  "comment": "TRAPEZOIDAL BUBBLE TILES, the 3-iamond family (Chase, Field & McCluer Appendix C, Figure 32). Three equilateral triangles in a row give an isosceles trapezoid with sides 1,1,1,2; reading the long base as two collinear unit edges makes it a weakly convex equilateral PENTAGON, angles 60/180/60/120/120 = 4/12/4/8/8 in D=24 units. The 180-degree corner is the point: it admits vertices where only TWO tiles meet, which is what widens the feasibility space in their Appendix A. No rotational period, so all 2^5 = 32 bite words are distinct tiles.",
